# harness run logs — the numbers live in the ticket, not in the repo
prototypes/webgl/harness/*.log
# …and the static server's own log, which the harness README tells you to redirect INTO the
# directory it is serving. `site/` is the deploy root, so an un-ignored httpd.log is a file that
# gets uploaded and publicly served. Found in 06 round 10.
site/httpd.log
# 02's originals — the files the masters were cut FROM. ~230 MB of museum JPEGs, re-fetchable at
# any time from sourced.json + orig/resolved.json, read only by the review surface. A local
# working set, not repo content, and the only thing here big enough to matter if it slipped in.
prototypes/directions/orig/
# lane A's second-opinion cuts and their comparison sheets — candidates, not masters, and
# reproducible from orig/ by rematte02.py. Nothing here is shippable until it is promoted.
prototypes/directions/alt/
prototypes/directions/rematte-sheet-*.png
# lane B's candidate pool: six photographs per `drop` key, their cuts, and the sheets they are
# chosen on. Same class as alt/ — a scratch pool, re-fetchable by resource02.py --find, and
# nothing in it reaches the site except through --promote, which writes img/ and sourced.json.
prototypes/directions/cand/
prototypes/directions/cand-sheet-*.png
prototypes/directions/cand-cut-sheet-*.png
prototypes/directions/cut02.log
# the third cut method's candidates and its sheet. Same class again — recut02.py rebuilds both
# from orig/, and a key only reaches img/ through --promote.
prototypes/directions/alt3/
prototypes/directions/recut02-sheet.png

